+**Windows note:** Set `HOME` in `.env` to your USERPROFILE path before running any `docker compose` command — Docker Compose uses `${HOME}` to resolve the GCP credentials path and `HOME` is not set as an OS env var on Windows. A commented placeholder (`# HOME=`) is already in `.env`.
+
+---
+
+## Workflow 1 — Local backend + containers
+
+Run Postgres and Elasticsearch in Docker; run the backend locally with Poetry. Preferred for backend development.
+
+**Step 1** — Clone the repo and enter the directory:
+```bash
+git clone <repo-url>
+cd codemie
+```
+
+**Step 2** — Edit `.env`:
+- Set your model provider credentials (e.g. `AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY`, `AZURE_OPENAI_URL`)
+- Windows only: uncomment `HOME=` and set it to your USERPROFILE path
+- Set `CALLBACK_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080`
+
+**Step 3** — Start Postgres and Elasticsearch:
+```bash
+docker compose up postgres elasticsearch
+```
+
+**Step 4** — Install Python dependencies:
+```bash
+poetry sync
+```
+
+**Step 5** — Apply database migrations:
+```bash
+make migrate
+```
+Raw command (fallback): `poetry run alembic -c src/external/alembic/alembic.ini upgrade head`
+
+**Step 6** — Start the backend:
+```bash
+make run
+```
+Raw command (fallback): `poetry run uvicorn codemie.rest_api.main:app --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8080 --reload`
+
+**Step 7** — Verify: open http://localhost:8080/docs
+
+---
+
+## Workflow 2 — Fully dockerized (for UI development)
+
+Everything runs in Docker. Best for UI development or fast first-run validation.
+
+**Step 1** — Clone the repo and enter the directory:
+```bash
+git clone <repo-url>
+cd codemie
+```
+
+**Step 2** — Edit `.env`:
+- Set your model provider credentials
+- Windows only: uncomment `HOME=` and set it to your USERPROFILE path
+
+**Step 3** — Start all services:
+```bash
+docker compose up --build codemie postgres elasticsearch
+```
+The build defaults to `INSTALL_ENTERPRISE=false` (OSS only). See Enterprise opt-in below if needed.
+
+**Step 4** — Verify: open http://localhost:8080/docs
+
+---
+
+## Enterprise opt-in (optional)
+
+Enterprise packages require access to the GCP Artifact Registry. To build with them:
+
+```bash
+docker compose build --build-arg INSTALL_ENTERPRISE=true codemie
+docker compose up codemie postgres elasticsearch
+```
+
+Prerequisites: valid GCP credentials at `${HOME}/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json`.
+
+---
