+---
+
+## Tasks
+
+### T1 — docker-compose.yml: change INSTALL_ENTERPRISE default to false
+
+**File**: `docker-compose.yml`
+
+Find the `codemie` service `build.args` block. Change the `INSTALL_ENTERPRISE` build arg default from `"true"` to `"false"`. Enterprise package installation requires GCP Artifact Registry access which standard developers do not have; OSS-only is the correct default.
+
+**Test-first**: no — Docker Compose build arg defaults are not covered by the test suite (all tests are fully mocked); the change is verified by inspecting the file.
+
+---
+
+### T2 — .env: add HOME placeholder for Windows
+
+**File**: `.env`
+
+Add a commented `HOME=` entry so Windows developers know to set it. Docker Compose resolves `${HOME}` (used in the `google_credentials` secret path) via `.env` on Windows, where `HOME` is not set as an OS env var.
+
+Add in a visible location (e.g. near the top of the file or alongside other local-dev prerequisites):
+
+```
+# Windows only: set HOME to your USERPROFILE path so docker compose resolves ${HOME}
+# Example: HOME=C:\Users\<your-username>
+# HOME=
+```
+
+**Test-first**: no — `.env` is a configuration file; the entry is a documentation comment.
+
+---
+
+### T3 — Makefile: add migrate target
+
+**File**: `Makefile`
+
+Add a `migrate` target that runs Alembic from the repo root, eliminating the OS-specific directory-change workaround. If the Makefile has a `.PHONY` declaration block, add `migrate` to it. If there is a help/usage target, add a `migrate` entry there too.
+
+```makefile
+migrate:
+	poetry run alembic -c src/external/alembic/alembic.ini upgrade head
+```
+
+**Test-first**: no — Makefile targets are not unit-tested; verified by running `make migrate` against a live local database during manual validation.
+
+---
+
+### T4 — .gitattributes: enforce LF for shell scripts
+
+**File**: `.gitattributes` (new file at repo root)
+
+Create `.gitattributes` to enforce LF line endings for `*.sh` files. Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows default) corrupts the shebang line of `scripts/git-hooks/pre_commit.sh` on Windows clone, producing "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" errors.
+
+```gitattributes
+# Enforce LF for shell scripts to prevent CRLF corruption on Windows clone
+*.sh text eol=lf
+```
+
+**Test-first**: no — git configuration file; effect verified by cloning on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true` and confirming the hook runs cleanly.
+
+---
+
+### T5 — README.md: two-workflow restructure, Windows commands, fix cd src/, add migration step
+
+**File**: `README.md`
+
+This is the largest change. Read the full current README first to understand the existing structure before editing.
+
+Sub-tasks in order:
+
+1. **Remove `cd src/`** instruction (currently around line 97). Replace with the correct invocation from repo root: `make run` (primary) or `poetry run uvicorn codemie.rest_api.main:app --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8080 --reload` (fallback).
+
+2. **Add `make migrate`** as an explicit numbered step in the Quick Start / local-dev flow, immediately before the "start the backend" step. Without migrations, the backend will fail on a fresh database.
+
+3. **Separate Workflow 1 and Workflow 2** into clearly labelled sections with explicit prerequisites and steps for each:
+   - **Workflow 1 — Local backend + containers**: start Postgres + ES in Docker, run backend locally. Include: Windows note for `HOME` in `.env`, `CALLBACK_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080` override note, `poetry sync` for environment setup.
+   - **Workflow 2 — Fully dockerized** (for UI development): `docker compose up --build codemie postgres elasticsearch`. Note `INSTALL_ENTERPRISE=false` default; add opt-in note with `--build-arg INSTALL_ENTERPRISE=true`.
+
+4. **Windows-compatible command alternatives**: for each bash-only developer-facing command, add a PowerShell equivalent inline or in a "Windows" note. Minimum required:
+   - `export VAR=value` → `$env:VAR = "value"`
+   - `chmod +x scripts/git-hooks/pre_commit.sh` → note this is not required on Windows (`.gitattributes` handles line endings; NTFS has no execute bit)
+   - Any `awk` / `grep` / shell pipeline used in developer-facing steps
+
+5. **Resolve contradictions**: scan for conflicting env var names, conflicting prerequisites, and inconsistent guidance between Workflow 1 and Workflow 2 sections; fix all occurrences found.
+
+**Test-first**: no — README is documentation; correctness verified by following the steps on a Windows machine and confirming both workflows succeed.
